{
  "requirement": "An evidence detail page MUST continue to show the current requirement or example and validation findings when evidence is missing or invalid. It MUST show readable placeholders for missing rationale or inputs and expose the contents of an unreadable JSON record.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** `requirements.index.invalid_detail` is met by the code in `src/index.rs`, and the tests cover its main cases.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `LoadedDetailEvidence::load` never aborts on bad evidence.\n  - A missing file gives `record = None` and the `Missing` state.\n  - Any other read error is added to the findings as \"cannot read evidence\".\n  - Invalid or unparseable JSON gives the `Invalid` state, and the raw record text is kept.\n  - Validation findings for the evidence file are collected from the report.\n- `render_detail_sections` always writes these parts, whatever the evidence state:\n  - the state badge;\n  - the quoted current requirement or example text (`## Requirement` or `## Example`);\n  - a `## Validation findings` section, shown whenever there are errors and HTML-escaped.\n- It uses readable placeholders: \"No rationale recorded.\" when the rationale is absent or blank, and \"No inputs recorded.\" when inputs are absent or empty.\n- When the record is not a parseable JSON object, it adds `## Unreadable evidence record` and prints the raw contents in a code block. `push_code_block` picks a fence longer than any backtick run in the text, so odd contents cannot break the block.\n\n**Tests**\n- `invalid_evidence_detail_remains_readable` renders a page directly for two cases.\n  - For a broken-JSON record (`{broken`) with findings, it asserts the definition text, the findings section, both placeholders, the unreadable-record section and the exact JSON code fence.\n  - For missing evidence, it asserts the definition text and both placeholders.\n- `index_lists_examples_and_links_their_detail_pages` covers a missing example end to end through `preprocess_book`. It asserts the example text, the \"Validation findings\" section with \"missing for example\", and \"No rationale recorded.\".\n- `index_shows_evidence_states_and_links_generated_chapters` covers the changed or invalid requirement. It asserts that the page shows \"requirement text changed\" and the current requirement text.\n\n**Gaps:** I did not find a test for the non-NotFound I/O error branch, or for valid JSON that is not an object. Both are small branches that reuse the same rendering path, so I don't count them as gaps.",
  "inputs": [
